00:26:11,949 --> 00:26:14,607
past the door of
 the round building,

765
00:26:14,607 --> 00:26:17,541
the entranceway to America.

766
00:26:17,541 --> 00:26:21,372
This is the ultimate
 answer, the ideal.

767
00:26:21,372 --> 00:26:22,546
This is what you've all--

768
00:26:22,546 --> 00:26:24,272
- [Mike] The cast of "Godspell."

769
00:26:24,272 --> 00:26:26,861
- [Woman Narrator] America,
 the land of beauty,

770
00:26:26,861 --> 00:26:29,691
where all your dreams
 will come true.

771
00:26:29,691 --> 00:26:30,554
- [Mike] America.

772
00:26:30,554 --> 00:26:31,797
- [Tom] Oh, America.

773
00:26:31,797 --> 00:26:33,212
- [Woman Narrator] You
 have all been trained.

774
00:26:33,212 --> 00:26:34,731
America,

775
00:26:34,731 --> 00:26:38,666
the happiness of your new world
forever, forever, forever!

776
00:26:38,666 --> 00:26:40,495
- [Tom] Oh, they blew their
 budget on the echo chamber.

777
00:26:40,495 --> 00:26:41,772
[applauding]

778
00:26:41,772 --> 00:26:44,016
- [Crow] America not
available in some areas.

779
00:26:44,016 --> 00:26:46,121
[applauding]

780
00:26:46,121 --> 00:26:47,364
- [Mike] Thank you,

781
00:26:47,364 --> 00:26:49,055
we'll now begin the
 Aunt Clara symposium.

782
00:26:49,055 --> 00:26:50,574
- Does anyone have
 any questions?

783
00:26:50,574 --> 00:26:52,956
- [Tom] Yeah, are you
 and Dick York friends?

784
00:26:52,956 --> 00:26:53,784
- Yes, Richard?

785
00:26:55,614 --> 00:26:58,306
- Dr. Jameson, I
 found something today

786
00:26:58,306 --> 00:27:00,549
that I think might
 be from America.

787
00:27:00,549 --> 00:27:02,586
It was floating in the river.

788
00:27:02,586 --> 00:27:03,518
- What is it?

789
00:27:03,518 --> 00:27:04,726
- [Crow] It's a Gambino, sir.

790
00:27:05,900 --> 00:27:07,453
- [Mike] Future
 anchorman, there.

791
00:27:09,282 --> 00:27:12,009
- [Tom] We chipped in
 and got you this beer.

792
00:27:12,009 --> 00:27:14,011
- This is not from America.

793
00:27:14,011 --> 00:27:15,495
It comes from the river.

794
00:27:15,495 --> 00:27:17,946
- [Crow] What, where you cloned
from a sack of doorknobs?

795
00:27:17,946 --> 00:27:20,224
- I'll just keep
 it for the museum.

796
00:27:20,224 --> 00:27:21,674
- But it's mine.

797
00:27:21,674 --> 00:27:22,848
- [Mike] You wanna watch "Sonny
& Cher" tonight, young man?

798
00:27:22,848 --> 00:27:26,023
- Richard, this
 belongs to all of us.

799
00:27:26,023 --> 00:27:27,646
- [Tom] Dick Sargent, Communist.

800
00:27:27,646 --> 00:27:28,474
- [Mike] Oooh.

801
00:27:28,474 --> 00:27:30,062
- Well, that's it.

802
00:27:30,062 --> 00:27:31,442
Good afternoon, all.

803
00:27:31,442 --> 00:27:33,099
If you have any
 further questions,

804
00:27:33,099 --> 00:27:34,825
please go to the confessional.

805
00:27:34,825 --> 00:27:36,724
[audience applauding]

806
00:27:36,724 --> 00:27:38,657
- [Crow] Stop that
 man, he has my can!

807
00:27:41,970 --> 00:27:44,870
- [Mike] Dick Sargent
 is the Bionic Woman.

808
00:27:44,870 --> 00:27:47,113
- Find out how this got
through the water valves

809
00:27:47,113 --> 00:27:49,771
and who the hell was
 in charge of cleanup?

810
00:27:49,771 --> 00:27:51,083
I want them out of here!

811
00:27:51,083 --> 00:27:52,360
- [Crow] Mr. York?

812
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:54,465
- [Mike] Mr. York, will
you sign this, Mr. York?

813
00:27:56,847 --> 00:27:59,332
- [Crow] Line up to hear
Firefall's latest hit.

814
00:28:00,851 --> 00:28:03,474
[somber music]

815
00:28:08,583 --> 00:28:09,929
- [Female Voice]
 How may we help you?

816
00:28:09,929 --> 00:28:11,137
- I have a question.

817
00:28:11,137 --> 00:28:12,725
- [Mike] I'll hang
 up and listen.

818
00:28:12,725 --> 00:28:17,626
- What does
M-I-L-W-A-U-K-E-E spell?

819
00:28:17,626 --> 00:28:18,558
- [Female Voice] Please wait.

820
00:28:18,558 --> 00:28:20,526
- [Tom] It spells $2.99 a case.

821
00:28:22,252 --> 00:28:25,220
- [Female Voice]
 M-I-L-W-A-U-K-E-E

822
00:28:25,220 --> 00:28:27,706
appears to be some sort
of nonsense spelling.

823
00:28:27,706 --> 00:28:30,605
- [Mike] Oh, it's Microsoft
 Spell Check by Phone.

824
00:28:30,605 --> 00:28:33,263
- Dr. Jameson told me it
 could be found in the river.

825
00:28:34,471 --> 00:28:35,714
- [Female Voiceover]
 One moment, please.

826
00:28:35,714 --> 00:28:38,164
- [Tom] Dr. Jameson
 is a big, dumb phony.

827
00:28:38,164 --> 00:28:39,683
- [Female Voiceover] There
 is a rare kind of mineral

828
00:28:39,683 --> 00:28:42,030
that is called "Milwaukee."

829
00:28:42,030 --> 00:28:45,137
It can only be found in
 certain parts of the river.

830
00:28:45,137 --> 00:28:46,690
- [Mike] Uh, do you buy that?

831
00:28:46,690 --> 00:28:48,796
- Can it be found in America?

832
00:28:48,796 --> 00:28:50,936
- [Female Voice] No, it can not.

833
00:28:50,936 --> 00:28:52,800
Is there anything else?

834
00:28:52,800 --> 00:28:54,215
- [Crow] Charles Van Dorken.

835
00:28:55,561 --> 00:28:58,357
- [Tom] They need better
funding for their language lab.

836
00:28:58,357 --> 00:29:00,531
- [Female Voice] I'm
glad we could help you.

837
00:29:02,671 --> 00:29:04,156
[Crow chuckling]

838
00:29:04,156 --> 00:29:07,746
- [Crow] You'd get better
 exercise sitting on a couch.

839
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:09,851
- [Mike] Daddy, Rex
 Tree, the Lumpy Man!

840
00:29:09,851 --> 00:29:11,991
[Crow and Tom laughing]

841
00:29:11,991 --> 00:29:13,234
- [Crow] The "go
 as slow as you can

842
00:29:13,234 --> 00:29:14,994
"without tipping over" race.

843
00:29:14,994 --> 00:29:17,134
[Tom giggling]

844
00:29:17,134 --> 00:29:19,896
[pleasant music]

845
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,070
- [Mike] A separate piece...

846
00:29:22,070 --> 00:29:23,037
Of crap!

847
00:29:23,037 --> 00:29:24,763
[Tom laughing]

848
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:25,867
- [Tom] Oh hi, Richard!

849
00:29:25,867 --> 00:29:26,730
- [Crow] Hey, Richard!

850
00:29:26,730 --> 00:29:27,662
- [Mike] Hi, Richard!

851
00:29:29,733 --> 00:29:31,079
- [Tom] The rare tree dork.

852
00:29:34,082 --> 00:29:35,739
- [Crow] Thanks
 for the subpoena.

853
00:29:37,051 --> 00:29:39,018
- [Mike] "Parts: The
 Visible Panty Line Horror."

854
00:29:39,018 --> 00:29:40,019
- [Tom] Ugh.

855
00:29:41,469 --> 00:29:43,505
- [Crow] The clone yards
 of Ernest and Julio Gallo.

856
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:46,439
- [Mike] We're
 done picking dirt.

857
00:29:47,751 --> 00:29:50,064
- [Tom] I guess Bing
Crosby was selling hats.

858
00:29:52,342 --> 00:29:56,173
- [Crow] It says, "Please
 help me down from this tree."

859
00:29:56,173 --> 00:29:58,037
- [Tom] Oh, a lock
 of his back hair.

860
00:30:00,729 --> 00:30:02,386
- [Mike] "Would you like
to share a quarter can

861
00:30:02,386 --> 00:30:04,388
"of water Old Mill with me?"

862
00:30:05,251 --> 00:30:08,772
[birds chirping]

863
00:30:08,772 --> 00:30:11,602
- [Tom] Oh, it's the refund
 for my nose job, good.

864
00:30:11,602 --> 00:30:12,880
- [Crow] Tome Jones, here.

865
00:30:15,883 --> 00:30:18,851
- [Mike] Okay, people,
 time to harvest more ticks.

866
00:30:18,851 --> 00:30:20,025
[whistle blowing]

867
00:30:20,025 --> 00:30:21,923
- [Tom] Bozo Circus
 is on the air!

868
00:30:21,923 --> 00:30:23,891
[singing circus tune]

869
00:30:23,891 --> 00:30:25,616
- [Lena] Hello, I'm Lena.

870
00:30:25,616 --> 00:30:26,859
- [Richard] I'm Richard.

871
00:30:26,859 --> 00:30:27,929
- [Crow] I'm Richard,
 I gotta remember that.

872
00:30:27,929 --> 00:30:29,620
I'm so bad with names.

873
00:30:29,620 --> 00:30:33,176
[crickets chirping]

874
00:30:33,176 --> 00:30:36,627
- [Mike] The scene was lit by
 an Indiglo watch apparently.

875
00:30:37,939 --> 00:30:38,906
- Hey.

876
00:30:38,906 --> 00:30:39,872
- [Tom] Kiss me, you feeb.

877
00:30:39,872 --> 00:30:41,149
- Why did you ask me here?

878
00:30:41,149 --> 00:30:42,668
- Because I wanted
 to talk to you.

879
00:30:42,668 --> 00:30:44,359
From the first day we met,

880
00:30:44,359 --> 00:30:46,741
I knew there was something
 different about you.

881
00:30:46,741 --> 00:30:47,569
- [Mike Deep Voice] There is?

882
00:30:47,569 --> 00:30:48,639
- You know what it is?

883
00:30:48,639 --> 00:30:49,778
Your eyes.

884
00:30:49,778 --> 00:30:50,987
They're so alive.

885
00:30:50,987 --> 00:30:52,851
- [Crow] Your
 nose, so truncated.

886
00:30:52,851 --> 00:30:54,438
- You know, I noticed
 the difference too.

887
00:30:54,438 --> 00:30:55,715
I mean, you're not
 like my friends.

888
00:30:55,715 --> 00:30:56,855
- [Tom] You're more icky.

889
00:30:56,855 --> 00:30:58,546
- Yours like mine, Richard.

890
00:30:58,546 --> 00:30:59,823
Why?

891
00:30:59,823 --> 00:31:01,894
- I don't know, Lena, I
asked the confessional

892
00:31:01,894 --> 00:31:04,483
and it just said that it
 was all part of the plan.

893
00:31:04,483 --> 00:31:05,933
- [Mike] Like Dan
 Fogelberg said.

894
00:31:05,933 --> 00:31:06,899
- Yeah, me too.

895
00:31:08,418 --> 00:31:09,281
- Hey.

896
00:31:09,281 --> 00:31:10,213
- What?

897
00:31:10,213 --> 00:31:11,386
- It's getting a little cold.

898
00:31:11,386 --> 00:31:13,285
How about some
 firewood and a fire?

899
00:31:13,285 --> 00:31:15,080
- [Crow] Mmm, she burns good.

900
00:31:15,080 --> 00:31:16,391
- [Richard] How long
 before you leave?

901
00:31:16,391 --> 00:31:17,634
- [Tom] Later on.

902
00:31:17,634 --> 00:31:19,118
- For America?

903
00:31:19,118 --> 00:31:19,947
Oh, I don't know.

904
00:31:20,879 --> 00:31:22,121
- [Mike] Watch your head there.

905
00:31:22,121 --> 00:31:23,951
- We go when it's time
 and when we're ready.

906
00:31:23,951 --> 00:31:25,366
- Yeah, that's
 what they tell us.

907
00:31:25,366 --> 00:31:26,194
Constantly.

908
00:31:27,644 --> 00:31:29,266
Where do you work, Lena?

909
00:31:29,266 --> 00:31:31,027
- I work in the [muffled word].

910
00:31:31,027 --> 00:31:32,269
- Huh?
 - Oh, I like it, it's nice.

911
00:31:32,269 --> 00:31:33,374
- [Mike] I like the
 [gibberish word].

912
00:31:33,374 --> 00:31:35,169
- Gives me time to write.

913
00:31:35,169 --> 00:31:36,515
- Write?

914
00:31:36,515 --> 00:31:38,275
- Yeah, I write my
 thoughts and my ideas.

915
00:31:38,275 --> 00:31:39,518
- [Crow] I've already
 filled a Post-it note.

916
00:31:39,518 --> 00:31:41,347
- It was my special
 place for writing.

917
00:31:42,383 --> 00:31:43,349
- It was?

918
00:31:43,349 --> 00:31:44,488
- [Tom] I'm not listening.

919
00:31:46,559 --> 00:31:47,595
- What's wrong?

920
00:31:47,595 --> 00:31:49,079
- Nothing's wrong.

921
00:31:49,079 --> 00:31:50,770
- Oh, come on, Lena, don't
 be like everyone else.

922
00:31:50,770 --> 00:31:52,358
You can tell me what's wrong.
 - Big slab.

923
00:31:52,358 --> 00:31:54,809
- Richard, we are not supposed
 to be talking like this.

924
00:31:54,809 --> 00:31:57,225
They told me it
 was not important.

925
00:31:57,225 --> 00:31:58,847
- What's not important?

926
00:31:58,847 --> 00:32:00,366
- [Crow] My gosh you're ugly.

927
00:32:01,885 --> 00:32:03,093
- His name was Allan

928
00:32:04,301 --> 00:32:06,510
and we met in compound
 four when we were 16.

929
00:32:06,510 --> 00:32:08,167
- [Mike] When I had a nose.

930
00:32:08,167 --> 00:32:09,444
- You know, he's
 beautiful, Richard.

931
00:32:09,444 --> 00:32:11,067
- [Tom] Not like you.

932
00:32:11,067 --> 00:32:13,172
- His hair was like the
 sun and his eye were green.

933
00:32:13,172 --> 00:32:14,691
No, he really was beautiful.

934
00:32:14,691 --> 00:32:16,624
- [Crow] There was this
 thing one time, I saw it.

935
00:32:16,624 --> 00:32:18,005
Boy, it was really neat too.

936
00:32:19,316 --> 00:32:22,319
- I never heard anybody
talk like that before.

937
00:32:22,319 --> 00:32:23,631
- Oh, I'm sorry, then I won't--

938
00:32:23,631 --> 00:32:25,081
- No, go on.

939
00:32:25,081 --> 00:32:28,532
- [Tom] I love it when you talk
about your other boyfriend.

940
00:32:28,532 --> 00:32:30,086
- He was a friend.

941
00:32:30,086 --> 00:32:31,259
I mean, we were in love.

942
00:32:31,259 --> 00:32:32,778
- [Crow] Right.

943
00:32:32,778 --> 00:32:33,952
- And when it came time
 for him to go to America,

944
00:32:33,952 --> 00:32:35,022
we asked if he could stay.

945
00:32:35,022 --> 00:32:35,919
- [Crow] Oh sure, sure.

946
00:32:35,919 --> 00:32:37,093
- They said no.

947
00:32:37,093 --> 00:32:38,611
And we asked if I could
go and they said no

948
00:32:38,611 --> 00:32:40,959
and finally they said he
 didn't have to go at all.

949
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:42,167
- [Crow] Uh-huh.

950
00:32:42,167 --> 00:32:43,685
- And?

951
00:32:43,685 --> 00:32:45,860
- And he disappeared.

952
00:32:45,860 --> 00:32:47,068
- [Crow] Huh?

953
00:32:47,068 --> 00:32:48,242
- No one knows anything,
not even his roommate.

954
00:32:48,242 --> 00:32:49,726
- [Mike] Let's
 crack the Pringles.

955
00:32:49,726 --> 00:32:51,797
- What must be must be.

956
00:32:51,797 --> 00:32:52,971
- Don't you get tired
 of hearing that?

957
00:32:52,971 --> 00:32:54,351
- [Crow] They're at EST camp.

958
00:32:56,284 --> 00:32:57,561
- [Lena] What's wrong?

959
00:32:57,561 --> 00:32:59,184
- I've never heard
 anyone say that.

960
00:32:59,184 --> 00:33:00,979
I mean, I've thought of that.

961
00:33:00,979 --> 00:33:02,152
- [Tom] I think.

962
00:33:02,152 --> 00:33:03,498
- But I've never
 heard anyone say it.

963
00:33:03,498 --> 00:33:06,363
Everyone here believes
 what must be must be.

964
00:33:06,363 --> 00:33:07,640
- Richard, stop!

965
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:10,160
We're not supposed to
 be talking like that.

966
00:33:10,160 --> 00:33:12,335
- Why? There's nobody
 within miles of us.

967
00:33:12,335 --> 00:33:14,164
- [Mike] I used "agree" today.

968
00:33:14,164 --> 00:33:15,890
- You know, you're right.

969
00:33:15,890 --> 00:33:17,098
[Tom chuckling]

970
00:33:17,098 --> 00:33:18,168
- You know, Lena?

971
00:33:18,168 --> 00:33:19,100
- What?

972
00:33:19,100 --> 00:33:20,308
- I love it when you laugh.

973
00:33:20,308 --> 00:33:21,758
- [Crow] Boy, if
 only you had a nose.

974
00:33:22,621 --> 00:33:23,449
- I like you.

975
00:33:23,449 --> 00:33:25,313
- [Tom] You have skin.

976
00:33:25,313 --> 00:33:27,660
[pleasant music]

977
00:33:27,660 --> 00:33:29,731
- I like you a lot.

978
00:33:29,731 --> 00:33:31,802
- [Mike] Look at that, he
 has really feminine hands.

979
00:33:31,802 --> 00:33:33,770
[Crow laughing]

980
00:33:33,770 --> 00:33:36,669
- [Crow] Shouldn't we wrestle
 and slap each other now?

981
00:33:36,669 --> 00:33:39,258
[upbeat music]

982
00:33:44,746 --> 00:33:46,748
- [Mike] I guess I gotta go
 a little easier next time.

983
00:33:46,748 --> 00:33:48,267
- You know, right
 before I met you,

984
00:33:48,267 --> 00:33:51,857
I found a piece of metal
and it had a word on it.

985
00:33:51,857 --> 00:33:54,549
- [Tom] Only you can
 prevent groin fires.

986
00:33:54,549 --> 00:33:55,723
- "Milwaukee."

987
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:59,140
And I asked...
 - Wow.

988
00:33:59,140 --> 00:34:01,729
- If it came from
 America and they said no.

989
00:34:01,729 --> 00:34:02,971
- [Crow] Hmmm.

990
00:34:02,971 --> 00:34:04,076
- And then I asked
 the confessional

991
00:34:05,250 --> 00:34:07,838
and it said it was a
 plant from the ocean.

992
00:34:07,838 --> 00:34:10,289
- [Crow] She really was
 on top of Ol' Smokey, huh?

993
00:34:10,289 --> 00:34:11,566
[Tom chuckling]

994
00:34:11,566 --> 00:34:13,051
- You know, when I
 was a little girl

995
00:34:13,051 --> 00:34:15,087
and I lived in the north
 section, I saw something.

996
00:34:15,087 --> 00:34:16,571
- [Mike] Wow, that's amazing.

997
00:34:17,434 --> 00:34:19,367
- One day, I was out playing

998
00:34:19,367 --> 00:34:21,059
and I saw one of the guide cars.

999
00:34:21,059 --> 00:34:22,577
- [Tom] Really?

1000
00:34:22,577 --> 00:34:23,509
- And there was something
 there that was covered,

1001
00:34:23,509 --> 00:34:26,167
so I was curious and a peeked.

1002
00:34:26,167 --> 00:34:27,444
- [Richard] And?

1003
00:34:27,444 --> 00:34:28,618
- [Tom] She looks like
 Henry Silva in a wig.

1004
00:34:28,618 --> 00:34:30,827
- I saw one of the
older members, Richard.

1005
00:34:30,827 --> 00:34:32,070
He was very still.

1006
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:34,210
- [Mike] She fell asleep
on dermabrasion wheel.

1007
00:34:34,210 --> 00:34:35,521
- [Crow] Ow.

1008
00:34:35,521 --> 00:34:36,626
- And they said he was asleep,

1009
00:34:36,626 --> 00:34:39,077
that sleep was very important.

1010
00:34:39,077 --> 00:34:40,975
But I'll never forget
 how odd it looked.

1011
00:34:40,975 --> 00:34:42,356
- [Tom] Do you like paper?

1012
00:34:42,356 --> 00:34:43,598
- We've gotta find out more.

1013
00:34:43,598 --> 00:34:45,083
- No.

1014
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:46,532
I'm frightened.

1015
00:34:46,532 --> 00:34:48,086
- I am too.

1016
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:49,604
But something's not right.

1017
00:34:51,019 --> 00:34:53,194
Unanswered questions,
 Lena, have to be answered.

1018
00:34:53,194 --> 00:34:55,921
- Richard, no, please.

1019
00:34:55,921 --> 00:34:57,992
I am frightened, you
 don't understand that.

1020
00:34:57,992 --> 00:34:59,442
- It'll be okay.

1021
00:34:59,442 --> 00:35:00,822
- [Mike] Come on, let's put
 out our flaming crotches

1022
00:35:00,822 --> 00:35:01,892
and we'll find your nose.

1023
00:35:01,892 --> 00:35:02,721
- Hey.

1024
00:35:03,653 --> 00:35:04,481
Trust me.

1025
00:35:04,481 --> 00:35:05,724
- [Crow] After all,

1026
00:35:05,724 --> 00:35:07,070
I look like the guy
 on "Three's Company."

1027
00:35:07,070 --> 00:35:08,313
- [Richard] Okay?

1028
00:35:08,313 --> 00:35:10,867
- [Mike] Is your face
 made out of clay or...

1029
00:35:10,867 --> 00:35:12,386
- Okay.

1030
00:35:12,386 --> 00:35:14,940
- [Tom] Now let's help Jack
 and Krissy move that couch.

1031
00:35:15,941 --> 00:35:17,115
[gunshot booming]
 - Ow!

1032
00:35:18,254 --> 00:35:22,810
[Mike, Crow and Tom
 huffing and groaning]

1033
00:35:24,156 --> 00:35:25,916
- [Mike] Des Moines Olympics
 are kind of a letdown,

1034
00:35:25,916 --> 00:35:27,332
aren't they?

1035
00:35:27,332 --> 00:35:28,816
- Richard.

1036
00:35:28,816 --> 00:35:30,335
Are you okay?

1037
00:35:30,335 --> 00:35:31,267
- I'm fine.

1038
00:35:31,267 --> 00:35:32,199
- [Crow] I'm just a puss.

1039
00:35:32,199 --> 00:35:33,579
- I see, well you slowed down.

1040
00:35:33,579 --> 00:35:35,616
I thought maybe it was
your ankle or something.

1041
00:35:35,616 --> 00:35:37,652
- No, I just slowed down.

1042
00:35:37,652 --> 00:35:38,619
- I don't understand.

1043
00:35:38,619 --> 00:35:40,690
You can't just slow down.

1044
00:35:40,690 --> 00:35:42,588
When you're in a
 race you have to win.

1045
00:35:43,762 --> 00:35:44,901
- Why?

1046
00:35:44,901 --> 00:35:46,351
- Why?

1047
00:35:46,351 --> 00:35:47,593
What kind of a question is that?

1048
00:35:47,593 --> 00:35:49,181
- [Tom] I'm just your
 Time Life operator.

1049
00:35:49,181 --> 00:35:51,045
- Why get involved
 in a race at all

1050
00:35:51,045 --> 00:35:52,253
if you're not gonna
give it all you've got?

1051
00:35:52,253 --> 00:35:54,013
- [Mike] Was this an
 after school special?

1052
00:35:54,013 --> 00:35:55,774
- I gave it all
 I wanted to give.

1053
00:35:55,774 --> 00:35:57,362
I just didn't feel like winning.

1054
00:35:58,225 --> 00:36:00,019
- I'll have to report this.

1055
00:36:00,019 --> 00:36:01,159
- To who?

1056
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,539
- [Crow] To the council
of loser clones.

1057
00:36:02,539 --> 00:36:03,782
- I'll have to report that too.

1058
00:36:03,782 --> 00:36:06,440
- [Tom] It's
 starting to stack up.

1059
00:36:06,440 --> 00:36:08,096
- Can I go now?

1060
00:36:08,096 --> 00:36:09,512
- Sure you can go.

1061
00:36:09,512 --> 00:36:11,203
- [Mike] Yeah, report my ass.

1062
00:36:11,203 --> 00:36:13,688
- [Tom] This is one of the
 12 Steve Prefontaine movies

1063
00:36:13,688 --> 00:36:15,345
being released this year.

1064
00:36:15,345 --> 00:36:16,174
It's great.

1065
00:36:17,209 --> 00:36:19,038
- [Mike] "Crotch Fires and You."

1066
00:36:20,488 --> 00:36:23,422
- [Tom] Let's see, "Jake
Cardigan pulled his hovercraft."

1067
00:36:24,527 --> 00:36:27,185
[ominous music]

1068
00:36:28,703 --> 00:36:31,603
- [Mike] Did I finish
 those cheese curls?

1069
00:36:31,603 --> 00:36:33,329
- [Tom] Doo, doo, doo.

1070
00:36:33,329 --> 00:36:34,916
[gasping]

1071
00:36:34,916 --> 00:36:36,366
- [Crow] I'm coming, Elizabeth.

1072
00:36:36,366 --> 00:36:37,298
I'm coming.

1073
00:36:37,298 --> 00:36:38,886
Elizabeth, I'm coming.

1074
00:36:38,886 --> 00:36:40,128
- [Mike] Feels like
 an elephant clone

1075
00:36:40,128 --> 00:36:42,269
is sitting on my chest.

1076
00:36:42,269 --> 00:36:44,271
- [Tom] The James Garner Story.

1077
00:36:45,306 --> 00:36:46,169
- [Crow] Beef.

1078
00:36:46,169 --> 00:36:48,344
It's what's for dinner.

1079
00:36:48,344 --> 00:36:49,862
Oh.

1080
00:36:49,862 --> 00:36:53,141
- [Mike] Hi, we're your
 heart attack consultants.

1081
00:36:53,141 --> 00:36:55,972
- [Tom] Let's get you out
 on that track, young man.

1082
00:36:55,972 --> 00:36:57,422
- [Mike] Oh, please be careful.

1083
00:36:57,422 --> 00:36:59,458
My chalky, spongy midsection.

1084
00:36:59,458 --> 00:37:02,150
[ominous music]

1085
00:37:02,150 --> 00:37:04,774
- [Crow] On Tuesdays you
 get extra prints for free!

1086
00:37:04,774 --> 00:37:07,432
- [Tom] God, the
 human body is hideous.

1087
00:37:07,432 --> 00:37:08,364
- Huh.

1088
00:37:08,364 --> 00:37:10,469
Well, I can't see anything.

1089
00:37:10,469 --> 00:37:11,919
- [Mike] You're dull
 and lumpy inside too.

1090
00:37:11,919 --> 00:37:13,817
- What did it feel like?

1091
00:37:13,817 --> 00:37:17,890
- It felt like a burning
sensation in my chest.

1092
00:37:17,890 --> 00:37:19,375
- [Crow] Well, Richard,

1093
00:37:19,375 --> 00:37:20,721
did you makes a run for
 the boarder earlier today?

1094
00:37:21,618 --> 00:37:23,068
- Are you sleeping okay?

1095
00:37:23,068 --> 00:37:24,897
- Sure, fine.

1096
00:37:24,897 --> 00:37:27,003
It just happened so quick,
 I don't know what it is.

1097
00:37:27,003 --> 00:37:28,763
- [Tom] Have you been
 eating your boogers?

1098
00:37:28,763 --> 00:37:30,662
- Let me ask you, Richard?

1099
00:37:30,662 --> 00:37:31,870
Do you spend a lot of
 time in the country?

1100
00:37:31,870 --> 00:37:33,872
- Or down by the river?

1101
00:37:34,873 --> 00:37:36,184
- No.

1102
00:37:36,184 --> 00:37:37,013
Why?

1103
00:37:37,013 --> 00:37:38,256
- Oh, no reason.

1104
00:37:38,256 --> 00:37:39,395
It's just that the
 air by the river

1105
00:37:39,395 --> 00:37:40,810
is not really very good for you.

1106
00:37:40,810 --> 00:37:41,742
- [Tom] Uh-huh.

1107
00:37:41,742 --> 00:37:42,674
- We just thought that it might

1108
00:37:42,674 --> 00:37:43,468
have something to do with it.

1109
00:37:43,468 --> 00:37:44,400
- [Mike] Am I dead?

1110
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:45,918
- What do you think it is?

1111
00:37:45,918 --> 00:37:48,024
- Oh, just a little attack
 of the nerves, I guess.

1112
00:37:48,024 --> 00:37:50,889
After all, you're probably
excited about going to America.

1113
00:37:50,889 --> 00:37:52,339
- [Tom] Today!

1114
00:37:52,339 --> 00:37:53,926
- Yes.

1115
00:37:53,926 --> 00:37:55,203
You're scheduled
 to go in two days.

1116
00:37:55,203 --> 00:37:56,688
- [Crow] We traded
 you to Cincinnati.

1117
00:37:56,688 --> 00:38:00,416
- We were going to wait but
you've been progressing so well,

1118
00:38:00,416 --> 00:38:02,210
we're letting you go early.

1119
00:38:02,210 --> 00:38:03,660
- Jeez.
 - Isn't that nice?

1120
00:38:03,660 --> 00:38:04,868
- [Mike] Ugh.

1121
00:38:04,868 --> 00:38:06,387
- Great.

1122
00:38:06,387 --> 00:38:08,872
- So why don't you go and
 get some sleep, all right?

1123
00:38:08,872 --> 00:38:11,081
Take these pills just
 before you go to bed,

1124
00:38:11,081 --> 00:38:12,462
I'm sure you're not going
 to have any trouble at all.

1125
00:38:12,462 --> 00:38:14,878
- [Mike] Can I bring
 my bike to America?

1126
00:38:14,878 --> 00:38:15,707
- Okay.

1127
00:38:18,054 --> 00:38:18,986
- [Tom] Nice gal.

1128
00:38:21,885 --> 00:38:24,232
- Well, did you hear enough?

1129
00:38:24,232 --> 00:38:25,441
- He's lying.

1130
00:38:25,441 --> 00:38:26,959
- [Crow] He looks
 like an adult fetus.

1131
00:38:28,271 --> 00:38:29,721
- [Mike] They found my nose!

1132
00:38:29,721 --> 00:38:31,964
- [Tom] The tight short
 clinic has been so much fun!

1133
00:38:31,964 --> 00:38:33,966
- I'm so happy to see you.

1134
00:38:33,966 --> 00:38:36,969
- [Crow] Allan and I are getting
married, isn't that great?!

1135
00:38:38,695 --> 00:38:40,110
- Lena, we're being watched.

1136
00:38:40,110 --> 00:38:41,595
- Richard, what're
 you talking about?

1137
00:38:41,595 --> 00:38:43,010
- I tried a test last night.

1138
00:38:43,010 --> 00:38:45,633
I pretended I was sick
when no one was around.

1139
00:38:45,633 --> 00:38:47,083
We are being watched.

1140
00:38:47,083 --> 00:38:48,153
- Richard, why
 would they watch us?

1141
00:38:48,153 --> 00:38:50,017
For what reason?

1142
00:38:50,017 --> 00:38:51,501
- [Richard] I don't know.

1143
00:38:51,501 --> 00:38:53,814
- [Mike] Maybe to see if
 we do that rubbing thing.

1144
00:38:53,814 --> 00:38:57,300
- [Tom] Let's go pray at the
 shrine of Dolly the sheep.

1145
00:38:57,300 --> 00:38:59,302
[wind howling]

1146
00:38:59,302 --> 00:39:01,580
- [Crow] Are you going
 to Bobby's America party?

1147
00:39:01,580 --> 00:39:03,444
- Lena, there's something
 strange happening here

1148
00:39:03,444 --> 00:39:05,135
that we're not
 allowed to know about.

1149
00:39:05,135 --> 00:39:06,309
- I know.

1150
00:39:06,309 --> 00:39:07,552
Richard, ever since
 you and I met,

1151
00:39:07,552 --> 00:39:09,485
the guides look at me strangely.

1152
00:39:09,485 --> 00:39:12,729
- Did you see the way they
looked at us when we first met?

1153
00:39:12,729 --> 00:39:13,558
They got angry.

1154
00:39:14,524 --> 00:39:16,008
- Speak to the confessional.

1155
00:39:16,008 --> 00:39:19,115
- I don't get any answers
 from the confessional.

1156
00:39:19,115 --> 00:39:21,082
I think the only place
 I'm gonna find any answers

1157
00:39:21,082 --> 00:39:21,876
is America.

1158
00:39:21,876 --> 00:39:23,119
- [Crow] Today!

1159
00:39:23,119 --> 00:39:24,223
- And I'm gonna try
 and get there tonight.

1160
00:39:24,223 --> 00:39:25,363
- [Crow] Or today!

1161
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:27,157
- But Richard,
 you're not qualified.

1162
00:39:27,157 --> 00:39:28,400
- Look, I saw the guides.

1163
00:39:28,400 --> 00:39:30,747
They took George up to
the building in the hill

1164
00:39:30,747 --> 00:39:32,128
after his party.

1165
00:39:32,128 --> 00:39:34,199
I think that's a
 good place to start.

1166
00:39:34,199 --> 00:39:35,407
I'm gonna try and get in.

1167
00:39:35,407 --> 00:39:36,960
- [Tom] If my SATs
 are good enough.

1168
00:39:38,583 --> 00:39:39,515
- No.

1169
00:39:39,515 --> 00:39:40,999
- [Crow] You and your big nose!

1170
00:39:43,001 --> 00:39:45,659
- [Mike] So you wanna take
 your shirt off now or...

1171
00:39:47,385 --> 00:39:49,248
- Lena, I have to go.

1172
00:39:49,248 --> 00:39:50,388
I've got to find out.

1173
00:39:51,699 --> 00:39:53,391
Don't be frightened.

1174
00:39:53,391 --> 00:39:55,462
- I am frightened, Richard.

1175
00:39:55,462 --> 00:39:56,808
I'm very frightened.

1176
00:39:57,878 --> 00:39:59,811
I'm never gonna see you again.

1177
00:39:59,811 --> 00:40:02,020
- Of course you're
 gonna see me again.

1178
00:40:02,020 --> 00:40:03,953
I'm gonna go to America,
find out the answers

1179
00:40:03,953 --> 00:40:04,850
and I'm gonna come back.

1180
00:40:04,850 --> 00:40:06,093
- Richard, why?

1181
00:40:06,093 --> 00:40:07,335
Why do you have
 to go to America?

1182
00:40:07,335 --> 00:40:08,544
- [Tom] Today!

1183
00:40:08,544 --> 00:40:10,269
- Because I have to find
out for you and for me

1184
00:40:10,269 --> 00:40:11,478
and for everyone else.

1185
00:40:11,478 --> 00:40:13,376
- [Crow] For the
 baby I'm carrying.

1186
00:40:13,376 --> 00:40:15,413
- Lena, you can't say
 anything to anybody.

1187
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:17,104
- [Tom] I'll leave you a
 lump of dough with hair on it

1188
00:40:17,104 --> 00:40:18,416
to remind you of me.

1189
00:40:18,416 --> 00:40:20,797
[dramatic music]
- Lena.

1190
00:40:20,797 --> 00:40:23,006
- [Mike] She's trying to
start his crotch on fire

1191
00:40:23,006 --> 00:40:23,869
with her mind.

1192
00:40:26,424 --> 00:40:29,185
- [Crow] Whoa, there
at Chuck Berry's ranch.

1193
00:40:29,185 --> 00:40:30,876
- [Tom] Aren't
 these stables phony?

1194
00:40:30,876 --> 00:40:33,948
[electrical buzzing]

1195
00:40:36,468 --> 00:40:39,264
- [Crow] Yeah, Secretariat
 is a personal friend of mine.

1196
00:40:42,094 --> 00:40:44,649
[upbeat music]

1197
00:40:48,687 --> 00:40:50,275
[singing tune]

1198
00:40:50,275 --> 00:40:51,897
- Ah, red!

1199
00:40:51,897 --> 00:40:53,520
- Hey, that was blue, I saw.

1200
00:40:53,520 --> 00:40:54,486
- No it wasn't.

1201
00:40:54,486 --> 00:40:55,660
- You're in the molasses swamp.

1202
00:40:55,660 --> 00:40:56,626
- I am not.

1203
00:40:56,626 --> 00:40:58,007
- Yeah, he's in molasses swamp.

1204
00:40:58,007 --> 00:40:59,905
- [Both] You're
 in molasses swamp!

1205
00:40:59,905 --> 00:41:01,079
You're in molasses swamp!

1206
00:41:01,079 --> 00:41:02,632
You're in molasses swamp!

1207
00:41:02,632 --> 00:41:03,771
- Mike...
 - You're in molasses swamp!

1208
00:41:03,771 --> 00:41:05,186
- You know me.

1209
00:41:05,186 --> 00:41:06,325
I'm a patient woman.
 - You're in molasses swamp!

1210
00:41:06,325 --> 00:41:07,154
- Shut up!

1211
00:41:08,845 --> 00:41:11,814
Oh, momma, do I need a break.

1212
00:41:11,814 --> 00:41:15,749
I sure could use that old
electronic babysitter right now.

1213
00:41:15,749 --> 00:41:19,062
So could you guys quick
whip up a TV show,

1214
00:41:19,062 --> 00:41:21,064
maybe one of them
 public kid shows.

1215
00:41:21,064 --> 00:41:22,341
You know, educational.

1216
00:41:22,341 --> 00:41:25,413
You know the kind of
crap I'm talking about.

1217
00:41:25,413 --> 00:41:26,794
[Bobo groaning]

1218
00:41:26,794 --> 00:41:27,933
[laughing]

1219
00:41:27,933 --> 00:41:30,626
- Ah, Mrs. Forrester,
 so you need me

1220
00:41:30,626 --> 00:41:33,421
and I have all the power.
 [laughing]

1221
00:41:33,421 --> 00:41:35,976
Once again you see there
 is nothing you can possess

1222
00:41:35,976 --> 00:41:38,081
which I cannot take away.

1223
00:41:38,081 --> 00:41:39,117
Too bad.

1224
00:41:39,117 --> 00:41:41,119
The Havidos could've warned you

1225
00:41:41,119 --> 00:41:42,845
if only you spoke Havidos.

1226
00:41:42,845 --> 00:41:45,433
[speaking foreign language]

1227
00:41:45,433 --> 00:41:46,400
- Ugh.

1228
00:41:46,400 --> 00:41:49,265
Oh, would you just help me out.

1229
00:41:49,265 --> 00:41:52,371
Hey, kids, "Satellite
 of Love" is on.

1230
00:41:52,371 --> 00:41:55,202
- Oh, I don't like
 that show, it's dumb.

1231
00:41:55,202 --> 00:41:56,755
- It's got robots.

1232
00:41:56,755 --> 00:41:59,309
- Robots are dumb, you're dumb.

1233
00:41:59,309 --> 00:42:01,898
- I took the liberty of
 making some fruit leather.

1234
00:42:01,898 --> 00:42:02,934
- What the hell is--

1235
00:42:02,934 --> 00:42:04,901
- [Kids] Fruit leather!

1236
00:42:04,901 --> 00:42:06,109
[chiming music]

1237
00:42:06,109 --> 00:42:10,286
♪ We'll have fun on
the Satellite of Love ♪

1238
00:42:10,286 --> 00:42:11,114
♪ Today

1239
00:42:11,114 --> 00:42:13,979
[giggling]

1240
00:42:13,979 --> 00:42:15,463
- Hi, kids!
 - Hi.

1241
00:42:15,463 --> 00:42:17,845
- I'm Crow the...

1242
00:42:17,845 --> 00:42:19,088
Cow.
 [laughing]

1243
00:42:19,088 --> 00:42:22,367
And this is Tommy the
 timid tuna, right.

1244
00:42:22,367 --> 00:42:23,195
- Aaaww.

1245
00:42:23,195 --> 00:42:24,611
- Today's letter...

1246
00:42:27,821 --> 00:42:28,649
- A.

1247
00:42:29,961 --> 00:42:30,789
- A?

1248
00:42:32,308 --> 00:42:33,930
- [Both] A!

1249
00:42:33,930 --> 00:42:35,863
[laughing]

1250
00:42:35,863 --> 00:42:38,556
[clearing throat]

1251
00:42:38,556 --> 00:42:40,247
- Today's number.

1252
00:42:42,456 --> 00:42:43,630
- Three.

1253
00:42:43,630 --> 00:42:44,492
[gasping]

1254
00:42:44,492 --> 00:42:45,666
- Three?

1255
00:42:45,666 --> 00:42:47,668
[laughing]

1256
00:42:47,668 --> 00:42:48,842
So today...

1257
00:42:48,842 --> 00:42:50,568
Today we learned...

1258
00:42:50,568 --> 00:42:52,086
- A

1259
00:42:52,086 --> 00:42:54,019
and three.

1260
00:42:54,019 --> 00:42:55,607
♪ Today we learned

1261
00:42:55,607 --> 00:42:57,229
♪ A and three

1262
00:42:57,229 --> 00:42:59,577
♪ Today we learned A and three

1263
00:42:59,577 --> 00:43:01,199
[laughing]

