2498
01:26:12,684 --> 01:26:13,823
- [Mike] Arrrr.

2499
01:26:13,823 --> 01:26:15,066
- Ladies and gentlemen
 of the press,

2500
01:26:15,066 --> 01:26:16,550
let's get right
 to the questions.

2501
01:26:16,550 --> 01:26:18,345
- [Tom] Who's coming up
 this week on "Biography?"

2502
01:26:18,345 --> 01:26:19,208
- Miss Grady.

2503
01:26:19,208 --> 01:26:20,175
- [Crow] Grady!

2504
01:26:20,175 --> 01:26:21,659
- [Grady] Senator Knight,

2505
01:26:21,659 --> 01:26:24,179
what will your position be on
 the subject of human rights?

2506
01:26:24,179 --> 01:26:26,181
- [Jeff] Well, you know, I
 talked a great deal about that

2507
01:26:26,181 --> 01:26:28,079
during the campaign but
I think it's important

2508
01:26:28,079 --> 01:26:29,184
to repeat it now.

2509
01:26:29,184 --> 01:26:31,116
As president, my
position will be

2510
01:26:31,116 --> 01:26:33,671
that any suppression of
rights or infringement--

2511
01:26:33,671 --> 01:26:34,775
- [Mike] Wow.

2512
01:26:34,775 --> 01:26:35,845
- [Crow] Mm-hmm.

2513
01:26:35,845 --> 01:26:37,192
- [Mike] Get it?!

2514
01:26:37,192 --> 01:26:38,434
[Tom giggling]

2515
01:26:38,434 --> 01:26:40,402
- As such cannot and
 will not be tolerated.

2516
01:26:40,402 --> 01:26:41,989
- [Crow] Senator, I'm
 Brown from the Sun.

2517
01:26:41,989 --> 01:26:43,128
- Senator!

2518
01:26:43,128 --> 01:26:44,475
- [Jeff] Yes,
 gentleman in the back.

2519
01:26:44,475 --> 01:26:45,579
- Bernie, Daily Sun.

2520
01:26:45,579 --> 01:26:47,063
- [Tom] I love Bridget.

2521
01:26:47,063 --> 01:26:48,824
- Senator could you please
 tell us about Clonus.

2522
01:26:50,722 --> 01:26:52,345
- [Mike] Arrrr?

2523
01:26:52,345 --> 01:26:53,346
- [Crow] Yes, definitely.

2524
01:26:53,346 --> 01:26:54,588
Um, Brit Hume, front row.

2525
01:26:56,901 --> 01:26:59,075
- [Tom] I can barely
 hear my heart beating.

2526
01:27:00,629 --> 01:27:02,700
- [Mike] I'm a sad clown.

2527
01:27:02,700 --> 01:27:05,220
- [Crow] Boy, that clock
never moves, does it?

2528
01:27:05,220 --> 01:27:06,807
[ominous music]

2529
01:27:06,807 --> 01:27:07,739
- [Tom] Was that a bad movie

2530
01:27:07,739 --> 01:27:09,189
or was I just in the wrong mood?

2531
01:27:09,189 --> 01:27:10,880
- [Crow] Oh, we can
 leave, all right!

2532
01:27:10,880 --> 01:27:11,709
- [Mike] Wait...

2533
01:27:11,709 --> 01:27:13,193
Oh.

2534
01:27:13,193 --> 01:27:14,367
Oh boy.

2535
01:27:14,367 --> 01:27:15,989
Executive producer,
 Walter Fiveson,

2536
01:27:15,989 --> 01:27:18,612
was a good friend of
 Supervising Executive Producer

2537
01:27:18,612 --> 01:27:19,751
Ray Dryden.

2538
01:27:19,751 --> 01:27:21,028
They grew up together
 in a log cabin

2539
01:27:21,028 --> 01:27:24,549
with a woman involved in
casting, Susan Arnold.

2540
01:27:24,549 --> 01:27:27,207
- [Tom] But all was
 not as it seemed.

2541
01:27:27,207 --> 01:27:29,382
- [Crow] The arrival
 of Associate Producer

2542
01:27:29,382 --> 01:27:32,833
Peter R.J. Deyell, proved
 both groundbreaking

2543
01:27:32,833 --> 01:27:36,147
and heart wrenching for
the young Liverpoolians.

2544
01:27:36,147 --> 01:27:38,529
- [Mike] And then
Co-Producer Michael Lee

2545
01:27:38,529 --> 01:27:41,428
and Carolyn Haber and Michael
 Lee and Paul Berkowitz

2546
01:27:41,428 --> 01:27:43,465
and Joe Gianonne
 and Robert Cummings

2547
01:27:43,465 --> 01:27:45,950
and Michael Lacoe
 and some other guys

2548
01:27:45,950 --> 01:27:47,020
and Harley Pence.

2549
01:27:47,020 --> 01:27:48,263
- [Tom] I'll take it, Mike.

2550
01:27:48,263 --> 01:27:50,368
The oddly named,
 Timaree McCormick,

2551
01:27:50,368 --> 01:27:52,059
young and brilliant
 production assistant,

2552
01:27:52,059 --> 01:27:55,097
developed an unhealthy
fixation of Joe Blasco,

2553
01:27:55,097 --> 01:27:57,272
founder of the Joe
 Blasco Makeup School.

2554
01:27:57,272 --> 01:27:58,825
- [Crow] I'll take it.

2555
01:27:58,825 --> 01:28:01,448
Dwight LaVers, a name known to
 millions, yet a dark mystery,

2556
01:28:01,448 --> 01:28:04,106
to even his closest friends.

2557
01:28:04,106 --> 01:28:05,866
- [Mike] Tomorrow,
 the fascinating world

2558
01:28:05,866 --> 01:28:09,042
of M.A "Ma" Schreibman who
 conquered his blindness

2559
01:28:09,042 --> 01:28:11,665
to become one of the most
sought after visual consultants

2560
01:28:11,665 --> 01:28:13,115
in the business.

2561
01:28:13,115 --> 01:28:14,910
- [Tom] The thin stylings
 of Brogan DePard...

2562
01:28:14,910 --> 01:28:16,360
Brogan...

2563
01:28:16,360 --> 01:28:18,603
Paul Sharp and Ted Keep,
 two crisply-named young men,

2564
01:28:18,603 --> 01:28:20,122
tonight on "Biography."

2565
01:28:21,261 --> 01:28:23,815
- [Crow] Freeze Frame,
 the J. Geils Band.

2566
01:28:23,815 --> 01:28:26,266
Synonyms in the hearts
of Americans everywhere.

2567
01:28:26,266 --> 01:28:28,475
[Mike laughing]

2568
01:28:28,475 --> 01:28:29,683
- [Mike] Ah!

2569
01:28:29,683 --> 01:28:31,892
Peter Graves, the
 underrated, underpaid

2570
01:28:31,892 --> 01:28:33,894
and incredibly handsome
host of "Biography,"

2571
01:28:33,894 --> 01:28:35,482
tonight on "Biography."

2572
01:28:35,482 --> 01:28:37,208
- [Crow] Tonight on "Biography,"

2573
01:28:37,208 --> 01:28:39,969
Paulette Breen who turned
 down perfectly innocent

2574
01:28:39,969 --> 01:28:41,971
sexually advances
 from Peter Graves

2575
01:28:41,971 --> 01:28:43,628
on the set of the
 movie "Clonus,"

2576
01:28:43,628 --> 01:28:45,803
who will never work
 in this town again.

2577
01:28:45,803 --> 01:28:47,977
- [Tom] James Mantell, in
 a striking coincidence,

2578
01:28:47,977 --> 01:28:50,359
shared a first name with
 the hulking, expressionless

2579
01:28:50,359 --> 01:28:52,568
pseudo cowboy, James Arness.

2580
01:28:52,568 --> 01:28:54,087
James Arness,

2581
01:28:54,087 --> 01:28:57,055
as a young boy, James Arness
 nurtured a howling bitterness

2582
01:28:57,055 --> 01:28:59,472
in the face of the
 awesomely superior talent

2583
01:28:59,472 --> 01:29:01,370
of his brother, Peter Graves.

2584
01:29:01,370 --> 01:29:03,372
Peter Graves' life
 and career were marked

2585
01:29:03,372 --> 01:29:06,168
by a generosity of spirit
 and loving attitude

2586
01:29:06,168 --> 01:29:08,412
towards his fell man, which
 were altogether missing

2587
01:29:08,412 --> 01:29:11,173
in the pitted soul
 if James Arness.

2588
01:29:11,173 --> 01:29:14,107
Often, James Arness' mother
 would remark to friends

2589
01:29:14,107 --> 01:29:17,697
that she loved her son, Peter
 Graves, so very, very much,

2590
01:29:17,697 --> 01:29:20,147
while she hates James
 Arness and cursed the day

2591
01:29:20,147 --> 01:29:22,633
her womb had been blighted
 with such a creature.

2592
01:29:22,633 --> 01:29:25,049
James Arness, ugly and stupid.

2593
01:29:25,049 --> 01:29:26,671
Tonight on "Biography."

2594
01:29:27,983 --> 01:29:29,225
- [Crow] Okay.

2595
01:29:29,225 --> 01:29:30,365
- [Mike] That's as
 good as it gets.

2596
01:29:30,365 --> 01:29:32,297
So, Peter Graves?
 - Biography.

2597
01:29:32,297 --> 01:29:33,609
- [Mike] Biography.

2598
01:29:33,609 --> 01:29:35,024
- Agua!

2599
01:29:35,024 --> 01:29:36,819
[rumbling]

2600
01:29:36,819 --> 01:29:38,683
[thudding]

2601
01:29:38,683 --> 01:29:40,823
[beeping]

2602
01:29:40,823 --> 01:29:42,618
[mechanical buzzing]

2603
01:29:42,618 --> 01:29:44,689
[chains rattling]

2604
01:29:44,689 --> 01:29:47,416
[buzzing]

2605
01:29:47,416 --> 01:29:49,867
[clearing throat]

2606
01:29:49,867 --> 01:29:52,628
So, what do you think
 of my new nose job?

2607
01:29:52,628 --> 01:29:54,699
- It's downright
Bruce Jennerian.

2608
01:29:54,699 --> 01:29:57,219
- Yes, well I went a little
 deeper than I might have

2609
01:29:57,219 --> 01:30:00,395
because I feel I can always
 add more later if I wanted.

2610
01:30:01,257 --> 01:30:03,052
- Mike, Bobo's calling.

2611
01:30:03,052 --> 01:30:05,365
- What're you looking at?

2612
01:30:05,365 --> 01:30:07,885
- Please, Mike, keep it quiet.

2613
01:30:07,885 --> 01:30:10,163
Evil orphan space
children were very fussy

2614
01:30:10,163 --> 01:30:11,406
getting down tonight.

2615
01:30:11,406 --> 01:30:14,167
I think they're
 off their routine.

2616
01:30:14,167 --> 01:30:16,756
- Aw, well I've
 got just the thing.

2617
01:30:16,756 --> 01:30:18,033
I wrote a little night music

2618
01:30:18,033 --> 01:30:20,138
inspired by a poem
 I've always loved.

2619
01:30:20,138 --> 01:30:24,419
The words are, "Sleep,
 oh fair one, sleep.

2620
01:30:24,419 --> 01:30:26,282
"The night is low and drowsy,

2621
01:30:26,282 --> 01:30:29,078
"your dreams are fair and deep.

2622
01:30:29,078 --> 01:30:33,117
"On feeble tender wings
rest all Earthly things.

2623
01:30:33,117 --> 01:30:35,222
"Sleep, oh gentle lamb,

2624
01:30:35,222 --> 01:30:38,294
"till morning mother
 sun does bring."

2625
01:30:38,294 --> 01:30:39,951
- That's beautiful.

2626
01:30:39,951 --> 01:30:40,745
- Okay, Mike.

2627
01:30:43,092 --> 01:30:46,993
[exciting marching band music]

2628
01:30:48,753 --> 01:30:50,583
[crying]

2629
01:30:50,583 --> 01:30:52,412
- You are so dead, Nelson!

2630
01:30:52,412 --> 01:30:55,311
It is a John Agar
 film festival for you!

2631
01:30:56,312 --> 01:30:57,797
[thudding]
 [groaning]

2632
01:30:57,797 --> 01:30:59,764
[crying]

2633
01:30:59,764 --> 01:31:02,249
[somber music]

2634
01:32:00,618 --> 01:32:01,481
- Sure.

